      "side": 1,
      "message": "[From Jetski review] Two questions/concerns here:\n\n1. `get_packages(host\u003dTarget.host(), targets\u003d[target])` downloads the Linux sysroot into `clang/sysroot` (or `clang/sysroot-focal`), and the commit message mentions downloading the sysroot, but `WriteGNNinja` never passes `--sysroot\u003d...` to `cflags` or `ldflags`. Is `--sysroot` intended to be added here (or in a follow-up CL), or should `build/gen.py` only download host clang for now?\n2. This `else` branch also runs on other platforms supported by `gen.py` (e.g. FreeBSD, OpenBSD, NetBSD, Haiku, Solaris, z/OS) and on environments without `cipd` installed (e.g. distro packagers running `build/gen.py` without setting `CXX`), where `Arch.target()`, `ensure_local()`, or `cipd_dir / \u0027bin/clang++\u0027` will fail. Should we only use `ensure_local` on supported hosts (Linux/macOS) and/or fall back to `clang++` / `ar` when `cipd` is not in `PATH`?",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "d6d9c79b991c7476484876f5cf72d6f3108f319f",
