      "side": 1,
      "message": "[From Jetski review] Nit: In a CIPD ensure file, `@Subdir` applies to all subsequent lines until the next `@Subdir` directive. Currently this works because `get_packages` sorts `path \u003d\u003d \u0027\u0027` first, but if `ensure_local` is ever called with a root package after a subdir package, omitting `@Subdir` when `subdir \u003d\u003d \u0027\u0027` would install the root packages into the previous subdir. Unconditionally emitting `lines.append(f\u0027@Subdir {subdir}\\n\u0027)` (an empty `@Subdir` resets to the root directory) would make this independent of input ordering.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "d6d9c79b991c7476484876f5cf72d6f3108f319f",
      "serverId": "c360c8e5-7aa8-3905-a7a0-810934766dac"
    },
