      "side": 1,
      "message": "[From Jetski review] Instead of putting `pinned.py` and `target.py` under `infra/recipe_modules/pinned/` and importing them into the recipe Python process, would it be simpler to keep this logic under `build/` (or in `build/gen.py`) and invoke it from `infra/recipes/gn.py` as a step after `git checkout`?\n\nDoing so would have several benefits:\n1. It avoids all the recipe module boilerplate (`__init__.py`, `api.py`, `examples/full.py`, expectations, `README.recipes.md`) and eliminates the need for `# pragma: no cover` throughout these files.\n2. `build/gen.py` wouldn\u0027t need to manipulate `sys.path` to import core `Platform`/`Target` classes from `infra/recipe_modules/`, and `pinned.py` wouldn\u0027t need the `try ... except ImportError` workaround.\n3. Most importantly, because recipes load `recipe_modules` from the committed recipe bundle before `src_dir` checks out the Gerrit patchset, CLs that update pinned versions in `infra/recipe_modules/pinned/pinned.py` won\u0027t take effect in `api.pinned.get_packages()` during CQ tryjobs unless the script is invoked from the checked-out `src_dir` after `git checkout`.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "d6d9c79b991c7476484876f5cf72d6f3108f319f",
